# Destination research

Read `.cursor/skills/destination-research/SKILL.md` before writing.

- Store facts in `research/<slug>/`. Do not edit `src/content` or `public/photos` in a research pass.
- One destination per pass. Keep the search-name slug.
- Unknown fees, hours, and dates stay `Check on arrival` and `UNSOURCED`.
- Set `STATUS.md` to `stored` only when all six sections have sources, including food streets, nightlife, and lifestyle.
- Do only the research lane the board claimed: base, attractions, food, nightlife, lifestyle, or context.
- Update `ops/board/places/<slug>.json` before you finish. A missing lane stays open. The first pass ends `needs_depth`. Do not mark the whole dossier stored.
- Stop when the dossier is stored. The next claimed stage on the board sets the page up.
